5. ONE SQUARE ROOT + TWO TRISECTIONS for each polygon with phi(n) = 36
   Q(cos 2pi/n) has degree 18 = 2 * 3^2; its tower is one quadratic and two cubic steps, each cubic step
   K(2cos(psi/3)) with 2cos(psi) in K (sections 3 and 4):
     37-gon:  sqrt(37)   c1 = 47/37 (rational);  c2 in K3 (nested, section 4)
     74-gon:  sqrt(37)   same field as the 37-gon
     57-gon:  sqrt(57)   c1 = 11/19 (rational);  c2 in K3 of the 19-gon (nested)
     76-gon:  sqrt(19)   as the 19-gon
    114-gon:  sqrt(57)   same field as the 57-gon
    108-gon:  sqrt(3)    c1 = -1 (psi = 120 deg, the 9-gon);  c2 = 2cos(2pi/9) (nested, the 27-gon)
     63-gon:  sqrt(21)   c1 = -13/7 (7-gon) and c2 = -1 (9-gon): two INDEPENDENT trisections of rational-cosine angles
    126-gon:  sqrt(21)   same field as the 63-gon
   quadratic subfields: conductor of Q(sqrt D) divides n in each case (37 | 37, 57 | 57, 76 | 76, 12 | 108, 21 | 63).

